  <h3>Figure 4.3 — EC2: running container and server logs</h3>
  <div class="figure">
    <div class="caption">What to capture: On the EC2 instance show: <code>docker ps</code> proving container is running, <code>docker logs --tail 200 fragments</code> showing server started, and the curl health JSON response.</div>
    <p>How to reproduce (on EC2):</p>
    <pre>sudo systemctl start docker
docker pull harshpahurkar/fragments:latest
docker run -d --name fragments -p 8080:8080 harshpahurkar/fragments:latest
docker ps --filter name=fragments
docker logs --tail 200 fragments
curl -i http://localhost:8080/health</pre>
    <p>Take screenshots of the terminal output for each of the above commands. The health response should be JSON with <code>status: "ok"</code> and the version fields.</p>
  </div>

