  <h2>5. How to reproduce & verify (concise checklist)</h2>
  <p>This section gives a concise, step-by-step guide a grader can follow to verify the API checklist items and evidence.</p>

  <h3>Preparation</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Clone the repo (private instructor repo or your private link):
      <pre>git clone &lt;private-repo-url&gt; fragments
cd fragments
</pre>
    </li>
    <li>Install dependencies and run unit tests locally:
      <pre>npm ci
npm test
npm run coverage</pre>
      Confirm tests pass and coverage summary is visible; screenshot it.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3>CI / Docker Hub verification</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Open GitHub Actions → select the latest <code>ci</code> run → verify the unit-tests job passed and the docker build/push step completed. Screenshot the build-push logs.</li>
    <li>Open Docker Hub (public URL) and confirm image tags (latest/main/sha) exist. Screenshot the tags page.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>EC2 run & API verification</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>SSH to EC2 instance and run the commands under Figure 4.3 to pull & run the container.</li>
    <li>Use curl to interact with health and API endpoints; screenshot responses showing headers and body. Example:
      <pre>curl -i http://localhost:8080/health
curl -i -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -u user1@email.com:password1 -d '{"a":1}' http://localhost:8080/v1/fragments
</pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

